# Pull requests that moved shipped source and deliberately carry no changelog
# entry. Read by scripts/changelog-completeness.mjs.
#
# One per line, `<number>: <reason>`. The reason is required: an exemption
# nobody can audit is how this gate would quietly stop meaning anything, so a
# bare number is an error rather than a skip. Every exemption that APPLIES is
# printed on a passing run too, so what was left out stays visible; one whose
# pull request falls outside the release being checked prints nothing.
#
# When this gate first ran, eight of 0.1.6's shipped-source merges sat here
# because the release had already shipped. Six of them described a change a
# consumer can see, so the 0.1.6 section and the published release notes were
# corrected to cite them rather than recording the gap as intended. What is
# left is the one pair that genuinely owes no entry.

352: reverted before release by #360, so the pair nets to no change
360: the revert of #352; the two diffs cancel on src/scanner.c, and the guard fixture landing with it is test-only
